1
00:02:04,781 --> 00:02:08,621
No living creature was hurt
during the production of this show.

2
00:02:10,791 --> 00:02:14,931
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

3
00:04:46,421 --> 00:04:48,011
Soldiers!

4
00:05:13,880 --> 00:05:15,670
God protect us all.

5
00:05:32,443 --> 00:05:34,333
Coming from that direction!

6
00:05:34,668 --> 00:05:36,508
Run! Run!

7
00:06:20,441 --> 00:06:22,831
Two Days Ago

8
00:06:29,238 --> 00:06:30,788
Hi all.

9
00:06:37,126 --> 00:06:38,586
Malhun Hatun.

10
00:06:40,070 --> 00:06:42,806
Where are these rugs going to?

11
00:06:42,806 --> 00:06:45,007
We will take them
to Harmankaya, Ayse Hatun.

12
00:06:45,007 --> 00:06:48,730
Why are you going to the infidels?
Let them pick up the rugs by themselves.

13
00:06:48,730 --> 00:06:52,710
This is Osman Bey's order.
This is not an aimless action, Ayse Hatun.

14
00:06:52,939 --> 00:06:55,009
We have a plan.

15
00:07:04,239 --> 00:07:07,219
We are ready to set off.

16
00:07:12,923 --> 00:07:17,023
Keep your eyes open, look sharp.
We are not going for a delivery.

17
00:07:17,176 --> 00:07:19,526
We are going to learn what's going on
in Harmankaya.

18
00:07:19,639 --> 00:07:20,969
Eyvallah. (Okay)

19
00:07:23,495 --> 00:07:25,785
It's time to conquest, Aygül.

20
00:07:26,960 --> 00:07:30,460
- Let's conquer the infidel from inside.
- Let's do it.

21
00:07:34,400 --> 00:07:36,140
You are entrusted to Allah.

22
00:07:36,140 --> 00:07:39,250
Go at once, come back at once
Inshallah.

23
00:07:39,250 --> 00:07:41,480
May your way be open, Inshallah.

24
00:07:41,587 --> 00:07:43,287
Eyvallah (thank you).

25
00:07:51,935 --> 00:07:53,215
Off we go.

26
00:08:37,836 --> 00:08:40,166
Bilecik Castle.

27
00:08:41,041 --> 00:08:44,631
Kayı's trading is about to stop...

28
00:08:45,330 --> 00:08:49,260
...while our caravans are all over
Bithynia.

29
00:08:50,912 --> 00:08:54,942
We gain power as Osman loses.

30
00:08:56,132 --> 00:08:59,692
To the unity of
the noble Lords of Bithynia.

31
00:08:59,750 --> 00:09:04,330
To us being able to have the Priest back.

32
00:09:05,466 --> 00:09:08,196
To Osman's defeat.

33
00:09:30,998 --> 00:09:33,318
Tell me about the problem,
Akca Dervish.

34
00:09:33,862 --> 00:09:35,782
It seems significant.

35
00:09:37,283 --> 00:09:42,473
My Bey, we have been trying to complete
the orders from Iznik for a long time...

36
00:09:43,080 --> 00:09:45,930
...but the orders remained unsold.

37
00:09:51,307 --> 00:09:55,375
Osman Bey, we wouldn't have spent
all our savings to complete the orders...

38
00:09:55,375 --> 00:09:57,185
if we hadn't trusted you.

39
00:09:59,574 --> 00:10:02,084
We made a great loss, Osman Bey.

40
00:10:02,669 --> 00:10:04,929
What are we going to do now, Osman Bey?

41
00:10:06,379 --> 00:10:08,939
Some of you are older than me.

42
00:10:10,536 --> 00:10:16,506
We haven't let anyone down since
my ancestor Ertugrul Ghazi.

43
00:10:17,692 --> 00:10:21,282
Don't worry.
Your loss will be covered.

44
00:10:22,320 --> 00:10:25,140
- We don't let anyone down.
- May Allah bless you.

45
00:10:25,908 --> 00:10:28,468
We knew you wouldn't
let us down, Osman Bey.

46
00:10:29,796 --> 00:10:31,686
May Allah Bless you too.

47
00:10:32,677 --> 00:10:34,087
Thank you all.

48
00:10:43,904 --> 00:10:46,484
They left my tradesmen in the lurch!

49
00:10:47,123 --> 00:10:49,733
I'll make them pay for it.

50
00:10:51,029 --> 00:10:54,349
You are known as the voice
of the oppressed, Osman Bey.

51
00:10:55,802 --> 00:11:00,912
You don't let your people down.
You make the cruels pay for what they do.

52
00:11:05,777 --> 00:11:08,217
You are going to get through this.

53
00:11:10,395 --> 00:11:13,255
I will, my Sheik, I will.

54
00:11:13,996 --> 00:11:16,026
Can I come in, my Sheik?

55
00:11:16,413 --> 00:11:18,653
Come my Boran Alp.

56
00:11:22,968 --> 00:11:25,918
My Bey, there's news from Rogatus.

57
00:11:27,048 --> 00:11:30,118
He invites you to his castle along with
the neighboring Lords.

58
00:11:33,031 --> 00:11:34,621
As you see, my Sheik.

59
00:11:36,621 --> 00:11:40,661
As you see, brother.
They want to reap what they sow.

60
00:11:43,115 --> 00:11:45,165
They want to discourage us.

61
00:11:48,423 --> 00:11:53,363
My Bey, our situation is apparent.
The thing to do is clear...

62
00:11:54,505 --> 00:11:56,695
...right, Osman Bey?

63
00:11:59,307 --> 00:12:01,597
The peace is good, Osman Bey.

64
00:12:07,691 --> 00:12:09,461
The thing to do is clear, brother.

65
00:12:11,446 --> 00:12:13,896
We'll accept the invitation.

66
00:12:15,919 --> 00:12:17,059
But...

67
00:12:19,543 --> 00:12:21,953
A guest mustn't be empty-handed.

68
00:12:22,901 --> 00:12:26,681
We'll bring them a present.

69
00:12:28,854 --> 00:12:31,434
We are going to make them pay.

70
00:12:33,272 --> 00:12:38,312
We are going to take revenge
for the oppressed.

71
00:12:43,124 --> 00:12:45,495
- Boran!
- My Bey.

72
00:12:45,495 --> 00:12:47,675
Let them know I accept their invitation.

73
00:12:48,292 --> 00:12:50,012
As you order, my Bey.

74
00:12:50,129 --> 00:12:51,519
My Sheik.

75
00:13:11,151 --> 00:13:13,681
Bilecik Castle.

76
00:13:14,647 --> 00:13:17,907
It was a great move, Rogatus.
I appreciate you.

77
00:13:19,435 --> 00:13:24,895
I can't wait to see
the desperate face of Osman.

78
00:13:26,762 --> 00:13:32,164
To be honest, the idea of seeing that
overweening Osman kneeling in front of us...

79
00:13:32,164 --> 00:13:35,424
excites me more than the idea of
having the Priest back.

80
00:13:36,787 --> 00:13:42,777
Osman will come here soon,
ready to surrender.

81
00:13:44,307 --> 00:13:47,857
We are all excited to see that.

82
00:14:34,862 --> 00:14:36,802
What are you doing, brother?

83
00:14:37,483 --> 00:14:39,323
I am scaling.

84
00:14:40,799 --> 00:14:45,719
I am previewing their
headless body, brother.

85
00:14:49,659 --> 00:14:51,769
Kayı's Bey Osman Bey is here.

86
00:15:25,663 --> 00:15:29,923
I appreciate that you accepted
my invitation, Osman Bey.

87
00:15:32,702 --> 00:15:36,082
You sent an invitation, and we are here.

88
00:15:40,848 --> 00:15:44,878
It's tradition,
we didn't come empty-handed.

89
00:16:19,262 --> 00:16:20,732
Feodor!

90
00:16:23,567 --> 00:16:24,807
Damn it!

91
00:16:29,974 --> 00:16:31,574
Damn it!

92
00:16:33,677 --> 00:16:35,637
What have you done, Osman Bey?

93
00:16:55,450 --> 00:16:59,790
You are not going to die before
experiencing the pain that I am...

94
00:17:00,241 --> 00:17:03,811
experiencing right now, Osman Bey.

95
00:17:06,884 --> 00:17:09,074
I wanted you to notice the truth.

96
00:17:12,637 --> 00:17:17,268
The truth is on the table which you wished
that I'd kneel in front of.

97
00:17:17,664 --> 00:17:22,634
If one disobeys Osman Bey,
he shall die!

98
00:17:31,404 --> 00:17:32,554
Listen to me now.

99
00:17:33,625 --> 00:17:37,745
You wanted to ruin me and many Turkmens.

100
00:17:44,721 --> 00:17:49,121
Do you think you can ruin Turks by
taking their gold away?

101
00:18:04,164 --> 00:18:06,304
Tit-for-tat.

102
00:18:07,208 --> 00:18:09,478
Your goods are mine.

103
00:18:10,169 --> 00:18:14,049
No one has peace if Turk has no peace.

104
00:18:14,667 --> 00:18:16,587
That's all I have to say.

105
00:18:42,715 --> 00:18:44,015
We're leaving.

106
00:19:00,907 --> 00:19:02,167
Osman.

107
00:19:03,088 --> 00:19:07,678
He always finds a way out.

108
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:10,440
Feodor.

109
00:19:12,266 --> 00:19:14,316
My loyal soldier.

110
00:19:20,713 --> 00:19:24,543
We are really sorry for Feodor, Rogatus.

111
00:19:26,338 --> 00:19:29,605
But there's even a more important
situation in front of us right now.

112
00:19:29,605 --> 00:19:32,145
- What can be more important, Kosses?
- Guess what!

113
00:19:36,044 --> 00:19:40,964
That Caravan, which carries
all of our goods...

114
00:19:40,964 --> 00:19:44,004
...has already departed from Damascus.

115
00:19:47,147 --> 00:19:52,477
Rogatus, don't let your anger
take over your brain.

116
00:19:54,386 --> 00:19:56,226
Osman...

117
00:19:56,654 --> 00:20:00,384
If Osman takes that too...

118
00:20:00,860 --> 00:20:03,084
He'll knock us down!

119
00:20:03,084 --> 00:20:05,294
I won't let this happen.

120
00:20:09,633 --> 00:20:12,553
I am going to protect the caravan.

121
00:20:16,412 --> 00:20:21,252
As we talked, Osman will come
around Castellion...

122
00:20:21,300 --> 00:20:24,890
and I, among us, know him the best.

123
00:20:28,382 --> 00:20:31,732
It's natural to know someone better when
he defeats you over and over again, I guess.

124
00:20:35,701 --> 00:20:40,081
You watched me losing
like watching a tragedy.

125
00:20:42,587 --> 00:20:47,867
Moreover, you left me alone
in front of Osman.

126
00:20:49,090 --> 00:20:54,150
Do you hold me responsible for all
of this now?

127
00:21:01,952 --> 00:21:04,842
I am sure you'll manage...

128
00:21:05,635 --> 00:21:06,995
Nicola.

129
00:21:12,788 --> 00:21:16,408
I, Aya Nicola...

130
00:21:16,781 --> 00:21:21,811
will not let Osman touch that caravan.

131
00:21:23,262 --> 00:21:25,532
I swear.

132
00:21:27,132 --> 00:21:28,832
I won't let him.

133
00:21:40,606 --> 00:21:44,276
Harmankaya Castle.

134
00:21:56,784 --> 00:22:00,264
Inform Mari.
We brought the rugs she wanted.

135
00:22:35,907 --> 00:22:37,977
Keep your eyes open Aygül.

136
00:22:38,594 --> 00:22:40,234
Let's do this.

137
00:22:50,187 --> 00:22:54,068
Malhun Hatun, what a surprise, welcome.

138
00:22:54,068 --> 00:22:55,708
Thank you Mari.

139
00:22:55,981 --> 00:22:58,461
I wanted to bring the rugs.

140
00:23:02,630 --> 00:23:04,460
You did fairly well.

141
00:23:05,270 --> 00:23:07,230
Meet Aygül.

142
00:23:07,316 --> 00:23:09,462
She is Osman Bey's cousin.

143
00:23:09,462 --> 00:23:12,322
Nice to meet you.
Welcome.

144
00:23:12,773 --> 00:23:14,163
Thank you.

145
00:23:16,150 --> 00:23:18,120
Let's get in.

146
00:23:45,374 --> 00:23:48,234
Sogut.

147
00:23:50,814 --> 00:23:52,804
From now on, the trophy...

148
00:23:53,427 --> 00:23:57,547
will be shared among the tradesmen
according to their loss...

149
00:23:59,587 --> 00:24:04,538
due to the broken agreements with Lords.

150
00:24:05,213 --> 00:24:06,813
Thank you, my Bey.

151
00:24:08,723 --> 00:24:11,403
We knew you wouldn't let us down,
Osman Bey.

152
00:24:11,403 --> 00:24:14,503
May Allah

153
00:24:14,527 --> 00:24:20,997
Don't worry. We'll find new trade routes
and make new treaties if needed.

154
00:24:23,069 --> 00:24:25,459
Be at ease.

155
00:24:26,350 --> 00:24:28,953
-Thank you, Osman Bey.
-May Allah bless you, Osman Bey.

156
00:24:28,953 --> 00:24:30,853
May Allah bless you too.

157
00:24:41,434 --> 00:24:42,924
Osman Bey.

158
00:24:45,660 --> 00:24:49,110
We've taken care of the problems
of the traders for now, thank Allah.

159
00:24:49,653 --> 00:24:54,933
But I must say it, until we find new
routes, the people will die.

160
00:24:55,264 --> 00:24:57,944
Who can we make treaties with, Osman Bey?

161
00:25:00,715 --> 00:25:04,845
Even if the heathens block one way,
we have a thousand other, brother.

162
00:25:05,072 --> 00:25:06,822
We'll find it.

163
00:25:14,327 --> 00:25:17,747
Harmankaya Castle

164
00:25:22,424 --> 00:25:24,614
Your sherbet is delicious.

165
00:25:24,855 --> 00:25:27,455
You brought it to Harmankaya.
Thank you.

166
00:25:27,915 --> 00:25:29,715
Enjoy it, Mari.

167
00:25:32,467 --> 00:25:35,389
That day, we couldn't show you
the carpets.

168
00:25:35,389 --> 00:25:38,109
For this reason, I wanted to bring
the completed ones.

169
00:25:38,167 --> 00:25:39,777
You are kind.

170
00:25:40,888 --> 00:25:45,888
It's actually good that not all of them
came at once. The lords don't know it.

171
00:25:46,742 --> 00:25:48,252
I know, of course.

172
00:25:50,505 --> 00:25:52,775
So, how will you take the rest?

173
00:25:53,106 --> 00:25:55,369
Will the lords allow this?

174
00:25:55,369 --> 00:25:57,749
There isn't a caravan coming soon.

175
00:25:58,768 --> 00:26:01,418
If there was, we would hide them there.

176
00:26:04,181 --> 00:26:06,631
The best is to wait.

177
00:26:08,103 --> 00:26:11,802
That big caravan from Damascus, carrying
all the goods of the lords.

178
00:26:11,802 --> 00:26:13,722
Isn't it coming soon?

179
00:26:30,702 --> 00:26:33,622
Let us bring them with that caravan, then.

180
00:26:33,622 --> 00:26:36,032
Unfortunately, Cornelia is mistaken.

181
00:26:37,199 --> 00:26:39,519
That caravan isn't passing through
Turkish lands.

182
00:26:39,723 --> 00:26:41,473
So, that won't do.

183
00:26:47,674 --> 00:26:49,794
Then, we'll wait for your word, Mari.

184
00:26:50,078 --> 00:26:52,448
We'll bring the rest when you want.

185
00:26:53,587 --> 00:26:54,687
If you allow us.

186
00:26:59,202 --> 00:27:03,212
Both our trade and friendship
please me. Stay in health.

187
00:27:03,704 --> 00:27:05,764
Likewise, Malhun Hatun.

188
00:27:05,882 --> 00:27:08,502
-You are always welcome here.
-Thank you.

189
00:27:37,946 --> 00:27:40,356
May Allah bless your hands,
my wife.

190
00:27:40,988 --> 00:27:42,658
Enjoy it.

191
00:27:51,344 --> 00:27:53,034
Cerkutay.

192
00:27:54,068 --> 00:27:56,038
Why aren't you eating, brother?

193
00:27:57,707 --> 00:27:59,477
Didn't you like it?

194
00:27:59,564 --> 00:28:04,104
No. When does Cerkutay ever not
like a meal?

195
00:28:06,069 --> 00:28:07,929
It looks delicious.

196
00:28:08,467 --> 00:28:09,617
So?

197
00:28:10,178 --> 00:28:13,998
But my throat is locked.

198
00:28:15,618 --> 00:28:17,228
Even water can't pass.

199
00:28:19,155 --> 00:28:21,515
What's your trouble, brother?

200
00:28:22,929 --> 00:28:25,439
It's like you've eaten lots of bulghur.

201
00:28:28,412 --> 00:28:29,902
Tell us.

202
00:28:32,892 --> 00:28:34,712
My trouble is great.

203
00:28:37,170 --> 00:28:39,450
And its cure is so pretty.

204
00:28:48,504 --> 00:28:52,574
I can't speak any words in front of
Aygül Hatun.

205
00:28:53,419 --> 00:28:55,179
I want to marry her.

206
00:28:57,140 --> 00:29:00,680
Tell me, how did you do this
marriage thing?

207
00:29:00,733 --> 00:29:02,723
Show me a way.

208
00:29:04,498 --> 00:29:06,938
Mine was so good.

209
00:29:09,085 --> 00:29:14,685
Boran is right. He was also like you
until he finally spoke of marriage.

210
00:29:32,485 --> 00:29:36,655
Brother, look. You will face her.

211
00:29:37,144 --> 00:29:38,904
You will say it in one breath.

212
00:29:39,013 --> 00:29:42,363
Without beating around the bush.

213
00:29:48,518 --> 00:29:50,298
In one breath?

214
00:29:53,096 --> 00:29:54,456
Yes.

215
00:30:01,313 --> 00:30:03,293
You are Cerkutay.

216
00:30:04,228 --> 00:30:05,818
Be brave.

217
00:30:06,855 --> 00:30:09,635
Face her and say it in one breath.

218
00:30:09,717 --> 00:30:11,517
I will say it in one breath!

219
00:30:18,928 --> 00:30:21,978
But the girl is crazy.

220
00:30:22,991 --> 00:30:26,441
Brother, inshallah she won't cut you.

221
00:30:32,912 --> 00:30:35,872
Even if she does, you'll say that
I died for love.

222
00:30:43,365 --> 00:30:47,005
Lovers don't die.
Neither does Cerkutay.

223
00:30:51,510 --> 00:30:53,550
In one breath, right?

224
00:30:53,819 --> 00:30:55,489
In one breath, brother.

225
00:30:56,154 --> 00:30:57,764
In one breath?

226
00:31:09,721 --> 00:31:11,319
It's delicious!

227
00:31:11,319 --> 00:31:13,089
Enjoy it.

228
00:31:16,381 --> 00:31:17,891
It's so good.

229
00:31:21,116 --> 00:31:22,116
So good.

230
00:31:26,865 --> 00:31:28,485
Look at you!

231
00:31:29,379 --> 00:31:31,819
Mashallah to my Orhan!
He grows so fast.

232
00:31:31,897 --> 00:31:35,507
Yes. He already grew
bigger than his clothes.

233
00:31:36,824 --> 00:31:39,204
Mashallah to my lion!

234
00:31:44,927 --> 00:31:47,667
We've overcome this as well, Bala Hatun.

235
00:31:48,711 --> 00:31:50,001
Thank Allah.

236
00:31:51,618 --> 00:31:54,978
This won't solve our problems but
it will ease them.

237
00:31:54,995 --> 00:31:56,855
It'll help the tribe.

238
00:31:56,921 --> 00:32:01,701
This was good. We relieved Osman Bey's
burdens, even if for a bit.

239
00:32:11,620 --> 00:32:13,350
Welcome, Osman Bey.

240
00:32:14,085 --> 00:32:16,362
Thank you.
Thank you.

241
00:32:16,362 --> 00:32:17,842
Welcome, my bey.

242
00:32:20,739 --> 00:32:22,909
Mashallah to my Orhan!

243
00:32:25,580 --> 00:32:28,210
Mashallah to my Orhan.
Mashallah.

244
00:32:33,060 --> 00:32:36,540
My bey, we delivered the carpets,
thank Allah.

245
00:32:37,130 --> 00:32:38,440
Thank you.

246
00:32:39,079 --> 00:32:40,879
Thank you.

247
00:32:44,806 --> 00:32:46,196
Let's see.

248
00:32:55,325 --> 00:32:57,385
Thank you, Malhun.

249
00:33:01,750 --> 00:33:03,593
So, Malhun.

250
00:33:03,593 --> 00:33:07,813
Tell me, what's the situation in
Harmankaya?

251
00:33:08,679 --> 00:33:10,899
Did you notice anything?

252
00:33:12,139 --> 00:33:14,039
How are the lords?

253
00:33:14,865 --> 00:33:17,255
Mari was pleased to see the carpets.

254
00:33:18,527 --> 00:33:23,107
She said that she can draw the curtain
without letting them notice anything.

255
00:33:24,819 --> 00:33:26,999
A great caravan is coming.

256
00:33:28,083 --> 00:33:31,853
It's an important caravan, my bey.
It's coming from Damascus.

257
00:33:33,191 --> 00:33:35,951
All lords have good in it.

258
00:33:36,955 --> 00:33:40,265
I knew that you wouldn't return
empty-handed, Malhun.

259
00:33:43,074 --> 00:33:45,524
Thank you.
Thank you.

260
00:33:49,193 --> 00:33:51,983
Now I will teach them a lesson.

261
00:33:53,047 --> 00:33:56,067
They'll see what does it mean to touch
a wolf's food.

262
00:33:57,269 --> 00:33:59,459
What's in your mind, Osman Bey?

263
00:33:59,780 --> 00:34:03,840
To do what's in my mind,
we need to use the priest.

264
00:34:05,390 --> 00:34:11,120
We put so much effort to take him.
Now it's time to use him.

265
00:34:14,505 --> 00:34:17,806
How is the priest, my bey?
Are his wounds healed?

266
00:34:18,219 --> 00:34:20,250
Kumral Abdal said that he is alright.

267
00:34:25,893 --> 00:34:27,513
Nikola.

268
00:34:30,489 --> 00:34:33,400
We have common enemies.

269
00:34:34,203 --> 00:34:36,463
So are our causes.

270
00:34:36,705 --> 00:34:39,165
And so should our ranks.

271
00:34:40,268 --> 00:34:43,339
Speak more clearly, Rogatus.
Please.

272
00:34:44,569 --> 00:34:46,324
These Palailogous'.

273
00:34:47,889 --> 00:34:50,600
They think nothing but themselves.

274
00:34:51,373 --> 00:34:54,342
There is nothing they can give you.

275
00:34:54,342 --> 00:34:57,363
I don't want you to be sure, Rogatus.

276
00:34:58,084 --> 00:35:00,395
After all, alliances aren't only
built...

277
00:35:00,395 --> 00:35:02,905
by wars.

278
00:35:12,114 --> 00:35:15,114
What's your offer, Rogatus?

279
00:35:22,950 --> 00:35:27,130
The thing that returned Priest Gregor
to Osman.

280
00:35:27,850 --> 00:35:35,361
This precious relic that Osman will
never give.

281
00:35:35,361 --> 00:35:37,221
A relic?

282
00:35:37,352 --> 00:35:39,162
What relic?

283
00:35:39,704 --> 00:35:43,314
We can only find out when we have it.

284
00:35:45,717 --> 00:35:49,827
We can only have it if we are together.

285
00:35:52,452 --> 00:35:54,872
I'll think about your offer, Rogatus.

286
00:35:55,957 --> 00:35:59,737
But there is something much more important
than this right now.

287
00:36:00,129 --> 00:36:03,766
It's the caravan that's important for
all our futures.

288
00:36:03,766 --> 00:36:06,846
I'm sure that you will protect
that caravan.

289
00:36:07,194 --> 00:36:09,574
Aya Nikola isn't alone now.

290
00:36:17,935 --> 00:36:21,805
Harmankaya Castle

291
00:36:27,535 --> 00:36:29,855
He isn't dead, huh?

292
00:36:37,243 --> 00:36:38,433
Is that so?

293
00:36:48,057 --> 00:36:49,217
So...

294
00:36:53,035 --> 00:36:55,475
where was he shot at that...

295
00:37:00,014 --> 00:37:02,744
he could survive, Bahadır?

296
00:37:04,141 --> 00:37:05,694
On his chest.

297
00:37:05,694 --> 00:37:07,954
On his chest...

298
00:37:17,104 --> 00:37:19,374
-On his shoulder!
-Oh, on his shoulder!

299
00:37:23,548 --> 00:37:25,498
On here?

300
00:37:27,260 --> 00:37:29,960
You don't even know where!

301
00:37:34,984 --> 00:37:37,834
Fortunately, your incapability
resulted well.

302
00:37:38,823 --> 00:37:41,393
It's good that the priest is alive.

303
00:37:44,901 --> 00:37:46,611
This is your reward.

304
00:37:49,928 --> 00:37:52,328
What's in your mind, Lord Kosses.

305
00:37:53,238 --> 00:37:56,938
There is a reason that priest
returned to Osman.

306
00:37:57,690 --> 00:38:00,060
Something he brought
from Constantinople.

307
00:38:00,344 --> 00:38:02,024
It's precious.

308
00:38:02,435 --> 00:38:06,085
You will find out what that is, Bahadır.

309
00:38:07,408 --> 00:38:09,128
Consider it done.

310
00:38:16,118 --> 00:38:17,538
I hope so...

311
00:38:17,982 --> 00:38:19,262
Bahadır.

312
00:38:19,986 --> 00:38:21,436
I hope so.

313
00:39:01,275 --> 00:39:03,485
Don't bother, Priest Efendi.

314
00:39:05,668 --> 00:39:09,028
I wanted to check your health.

315
00:39:10,196 --> 00:39:12,636
I'm grateful for your concern.

316
00:39:13,505 --> 00:39:15,535
But why am I here?

317
00:39:16,500 --> 00:39:18,210
Where is Osman Bey?

318
00:39:24,651 --> 00:39:27,931
You will be our guest in our lodge
for a while.

319
00:39:35,420 --> 00:39:38,430
With the name of Allah.

320
00:39:47,340 --> 00:39:48,890
This...

321
00:39:49,462 --> 00:39:51,352
It's vinegared water.

322
00:39:58,619 --> 00:40:00,999
With the name of Allah.

323
00:40:10,384 --> 00:40:12,594
And this is honeyed water.

324
00:40:15,536 --> 00:40:17,486
Both are healing.

325
00:40:18,625 --> 00:40:22,075
When you take them together,
they are even better.

326
00:40:25,148 --> 00:40:26,778
Not yet, Priest Efendi.

327
00:40:27,566 --> 00:40:29,296
There is time.

328
00:40:30,338 --> 00:40:32,888
This was the most delicious honey
I've ever tasted.

329
00:40:34,909 --> 00:40:39,959
What makes the honey so delicious is
the vinegar you drank before it.

330
00:41:21,485 --> 00:41:24,425
Look at Osman Bey's hawks.

331
00:41:28,971 --> 00:41:30,641
Cerkutay.

332
00:41:33,321 --> 00:41:35,081
Cerkutay.

333
00:41:39,187 --> 00:41:42,487
It's not important but very
important at the same time.

334
00:41:46,121 --> 00:41:50,051
Forget about it now. When will we
take the other heads?

335
00:41:53,724 --> 00:41:55,614
You are impatient, right?

336
00:41:56,999 --> 00:41:59,619
The time will come, brother.

337
00:42:01,190 --> 00:42:04,690
We'll take their heads and
their castles.

338
00:42:06,419 --> 00:42:09,499
We'll take them all.
We'll make it our home.

339
00:42:10,038 --> 00:42:11,458
Inshallah.

340
00:42:12,220 --> 00:42:16,680
Brothers, this is conquest.
Its time will come.

341
00:42:17,969 --> 00:42:21,269
Until that time, you will
be patient, brother.

342
00:42:22,419 --> 00:42:24,549
You tell them.

343
00:42:27,916 --> 00:42:31,066
These weapons wouldn't stay tamed
with Bamsı Bey either.

344
00:42:36,393 --> 00:42:39,263
They turn blunt if you don't wet
them with blood.

345
00:42:39,599 --> 00:42:43,779
Then, Osman Bey should run us
for one battle after another.

346
00:42:47,910 --> 00:42:53,530
So, Boran. You said conquest
and battle.

347
00:42:55,627 --> 00:42:57,567
Sing us a song.

348
00:42:57,902 --> 00:43:00,772
-Yeah?
-Yeah.

349
00:43:00,772 --> 00:43:01,782
Yes.

350
00:43:02,802 --> 00:43:05,612
Baykurt, come on.

351
00:43:10,244 --> 00:43:12,124
With the name of Allah.

352
00:43:27,372 --> 00:43:30,602
When you turned twenty...

353
00:43:31,797 --> 00:43:35,107
He saw a sacred dream.

354
00:43:36,280 --> 00:43:39,720
Against all the tyrants...

355
00:43:41,713 --> 00:43:44,813
he is a hidden menace, Osman Bey!

356
00:43:45,309 --> 00:43:48,769
He is a student of Edebali...

357
00:43:49,831 --> 00:43:53,381
may the heathens be cursed...

358
00:43:54,991 --> 00:43:58,271
he is the pride of Ertuğrul Ghazi...

359
00:43:59,463 --> 00:44:02,683
Osman Bey is a different valiant!

360
00:44:08,800 --> 00:44:12,510
He subdued many nations.

361
00:44:16,418 --> 00:44:19,458
The sky cried on red banners.

362
00:44:21,076 --> 00:44:24,236
He swung his claws on the tyrants.

363
00:44:25,442 --> 00:44:28,452
Like a black wolf, Osman Bey!

364
00:44:30,022 --> 00:44:33,132
He swung his claws on the tyrants.

365
00:44:34,382 --> 00:44:37,662
Like a black wolf, Osman Bey!

366
00:44:57,726 --> 00:45:01,036
On strong horses with
grey manes...

367
00:45:02,066 --> 00:45:05,636
with tough armors and
sharp weapons...

368
00:45:07,102 --> 00:45:10,072
with brave alps...

369
00:45:11,822 --> 00:45:14,812
He wrote an epic, Osman Bey!

370
00:45:16,475 --> 00:45:19,635
When the oppressed were crying...

371
00:45:20,842 --> 00:45:24,132
the ground has shaken from
the call...

372
00:45:25,474 --> 00:45:28,774
and a man emerged from its heart...

373
00:45:30,226 --> 00:45:33,186
like a majestic tent, Osman Bey!

374
00:45:39,835 --> 00:45:43,415
He subdued many nations.

375
00:45:47,614 --> 00:45:50,594
The sky cried on red banners.

376
00:45:51,736 --> 00:45:54,576
He swung his claws on tyrants.

377
00:45:55,697 --> 00:45:59,077
Like a black wolf, Osman Bey!

378
00:46:00,819 --> 00:46:03,789
He swung his claws on tyrants.

379
00:46:05,418 --> 00:46:08,558
Like a black wolf, Osman Bey!

380
00:46:22,057 --> 00:46:24,177
Mashallah, brother.

381
00:46:24,227 --> 00:46:26,257
Thank you, brother Boran.

382
00:46:30,098 --> 00:46:32,138
Cerkutay, don't eat it.

383
00:47:02,425 --> 00:47:04,355
Allahu Akbar.

384
00:47:05,272 --> 00:47:09,837
Allahu Akbar.

385
00:47:11,077 --> 00:47:12,957
Allahu Akbar.

386
00:47:35,193 --> 00:47:37,653
May the peace, mercy, and blessings
of Allah be with you.

387
00:47:38,787 --> 00:47:41,897
May the peace, mercy, and blessings
of Allah be with you.

388
00:47:52,326 --> 00:47:53,706
My Allah!

389
00:47:55,899 --> 00:47:58,689
For your most precious name.

390
00:48:00,791 --> 00:48:03,701
For the holiness of Celali.

391
00:48:06,428 --> 00:48:09,348
For the greatest name.

392
00:48:11,610 --> 00:48:14,010
For your prophets.

393
00:48:17,366 --> 00:48:20,076
For their parents.

394
00:48:21,798 --> 00:48:24,558
For the blood of the martyrs.

395
00:48:25,990 --> 00:48:29,180
Accept my gratitude.

396
00:48:32,965 --> 00:48:38,645
I don't have anything worthy
of your justice.

397
00:48:41,482 --> 00:48:44,122
You treat me with your mercy.

398
00:48:47,411 --> 00:48:50,411
Oh my Allah, mightiest of
the mighties.

399
00:48:52,668 --> 00:48:55,038
You are capable of everything.

400
00:48:56,761 --> 00:49:01,961
You destined us to pass the traps
of the heathens...

401
00:49:02,856 --> 00:49:05,146
through your wisdom.

402
00:49:06,217 --> 00:49:09,427
I opened my arms to worship you.

403
00:49:11,994 --> 00:49:14,044
Accept it, my Allah.

404
00:49:18,036 --> 00:49:21,156
Oh, the owner of everything!

405
00:49:23,844 --> 00:49:26,804
My jihad is for you.

406
00:49:29,034 --> 00:49:31,414
The sword I swing is for you.

407
00:49:34,152 --> 00:49:37,872
It's to have your name rule
over the world.

408
00:49:40,569 --> 00:49:42,789
To reach this holy dream...

409
00:49:45,355 --> 00:49:47,955
give me and my lineage strength.

410
00:49:50,444 --> 00:49:55,654
To beat the heathens,
give us strength.

411
00:49:57,292 --> 00:50:02,992
Bless us to ruin their traps...

412
00:50:04,289 --> 00:50:06,409
...that they set for us, Lord.

413
00:50:07,157 --> 00:50:09,137
Triumph is yours.

414
00:50:10,153 --> 00:50:12,753
Make us victorious!

415
00:50:24,008 --> 00:50:25,348
Amin.

416
00:51:27,457 --> 00:51:28,997
Salam Aleikum.

417
00:51:29,908 --> 00:51:32,678
Alaikum Salam.
Alaikum Salam.

418
00:51:33,923 --> 00:51:36,053
Inform Osman Bey.

419
00:51:36,364 --> 00:51:38,304
We brought a present.

420
00:51:39,245 --> 00:51:41,235
We will hand it in.

421
00:51:41,235 --> 00:51:45,285
It's important.
I want to deliver myself.

422
00:51:50,266 --> 00:51:52,226
Do not keep me waiting.

423
00:52:21,803 --> 00:52:23,353
Turgut Bey!

424
00:52:49,942 --> 00:52:52,862
I heard you let your alps hunt Catalans.

425
00:52:59,452 --> 00:53:02,012
But things didn't go well.

426
00:53:05,449 --> 00:53:08,929
I had a problem with the Catalans.

427
00:53:10,963 --> 00:53:12,643
So, I did it right.

428
00:53:20,238 --> 00:53:22,168
Mashallah (praise be).

429
00:53:23,449 --> 00:53:25,489
You showed how valiant you are.

430
00:53:30,512 --> 00:53:32,812
They lost their lives.

431
00:53:33,867 --> 00:53:36,077
We had a common enemy.

432
00:53:39,124 --> 00:53:42,474
That's right.
We had a common enemy.

433
00:53:43,682 --> 00:53:46,332
And every valiant needs a friend like you.

434
00:53:48,736 --> 00:53:50,646
Thank you.

435
00:53:54,045 --> 00:53:56,055
Not only them.

436
00:53:56,598 --> 00:54:00,678
I will have much more to do for you after
what you have done for my tent, Osman Bey.

437
00:54:00,888 --> 00:54:03,328
Everything has its time.

438
00:54:11,169 --> 00:54:12,899
Eyvallah(see you) then.

439
00:54:14,949 --> 00:54:17,129
Wait, Turgut Bey.

440
00:54:23,667 --> 00:54:25,417
Wait there.

441
00:54:26,472 --> 00:54:27,432
Goktug.

442
00:54:30,990 --> 00:54:33,970
Bring the share of Turgut Bey
from the trophy.

443
00:54:36,683 --> 00:54:38,363
As you order, my Bey.

444
00:54:40,830 --> 00:54:42,300
Horses!

445
00:54:53,824 --> 00:54:58,874
While you were fighting the enemy,
we finished them on the table.

446
00:55:00,756 --> 00:55:02,846
We reserved your share, Turgut Bey.

447
00:55:07,087 --> 00:55:08,647
Thank you.

448
00:55:25,607 --> 00:55:28,187
He is trying to suppress us.

449
00:55:29,986 --> 00:55:33,286
We should have been the ones who
brought the bodies of Catalans, brother.

450
00:55:41,403 --> 00:55:44,903
Goktug, let it be, brother.

451
00:55:46,904 --> 00:55:49,804
The betrayers are dead now.
Focus on the result.

452
00:55:50,509 --> 00:55:52,689
Why would we be upset?

453
00:55:54,766 --> 00:55:57,376
Right, right brother.

454
00:56:01,377 --> 00:56:04,617
Harmankaya Castle.

455
00:56:09,866 --> 00:56:13,916
We hosted Malhun Hatun very well.
She left satisfied.

456
00:56:23,637 --> 00:56:28,577
However, you have to hear what you
are saying. Remember they are our enemy.

457
00:56:30,258 --> 00:56:31,928
You are right, mistress.

458
00:56:37,781 --> 00:56:39,461
Brother?

459
00:56:50,330 --> 00:56:53,410
Why was Osman's Hatun here, Mari?

460
00:56:53,724 --> 00:56:56,604
How dare you do business without
my information?

461
00:56:57,533 --> 00:57:00,883
- Only for trade.
- What trade are you talking about, Mari?

462
00:57:02,517 --> 00:57:07,197
We made an agreement with the Lords to defeat
Osman! What trade are you talking about?

463
00:57:07,619 --> 00:57:10,979
I strongly remind you that I have
the same blood as you!

464
00:57:10,979 --> 00:57:12,548
I am making my own plan!

465
00:57:12,548 --> 00:57:16,238
How dare you make a plan
while I am alive!

466
00:57:18,696 --> 00:57:22,109
Where are you going?
I am not done!

467
00:57:22,109 --> 00:57:24,149
I am done!

468
00:57:25,400 --> 00:57:29,730
I am going hunting! I don't think I will
come back until I calm down!

469
00:57:34,062 --> 00:57:37,282
God knows the best.

470
00:58:38,905 --> 00:58:40,475
Hello there.

471
00:58:44,720 --> 00:58:46,410
Thank you.

472
00:58:52,329 --> 00:58:54,969
Do you know where Aygül Hatun is?

473
00:58:59,090 --> 00:59:02,020
What are you talking about?
Crazy! I am here.

474
00:59:03,648 --> 00:59:04,758
No.

475
00:59:06,791 --> 00:59:10,501
I am talking about the Aygül Hatun who
rises her sword...

476
00:59:10,844 --> 00:59:16,574
shoots arrows, knocks out seven men
all alone.

477
00:59:24,093 --> 00:59:26,183
Who were you talking about?

478
00:59:29,911 --> 00:59:32,151
That dagger won't harm me.

479
00:59:34,216 --> 00:59:38,586
Your looks that are sharper than a dagger
have already killed me, you tough girl.

480
01:00:14,526 --> 01:00:17,426
Do you know what that is?

481
01:00:21,616 --> 01:00:22,962
What is that?

482
01:00:27,089 --> 01:00:29,819
This is a flower.

483
01:00:33,820 --> 01:00:35,590
Are you serious?

484
01:00:59,233 --> 01:01:02,713
When someone gives this to you...

485
01:01:04,677 --> 01:01:06,347
something happens.

486
01:01:06,866 --> 01:01:08,566
What is that?

487
01:01:12,366 --> 01:01:13,806
Something.

488
01:01:14,094 --> 01:01:15,984
What is that, Cerkutay?

489
01:01:17,493 --> 01:01:21,463
Cerkutay, why are you keeping me
if you can't tell what it is!

490
01:01:21,894 --> 01:01:23,934
Get out of my way!

491
01:01:37,972 --> 01:01:39,692
Something happens.

492
01:01:43,671 --> 01:01:45,141
Yes.

493
01:01:46,813 --> 01:01:52,213
It's hard to talk when you are
a lover with a burning heart.

494
01:02:27,149 --> 01:02:29,509
Sogut.

495
01:02:31,393 --> 01:02:35,133
Our beautifully named glorious
prophet...

496
01:02:35,199 --> 01:02:39,139
Hadrat Muhammed Mustafa...

497
01:02:39,139 --> 01:02:41,976
"Peace be upon him."

498
01:02:41,976 --> 01:02:44,816
Hadrat Isa (Jesus) was before Him.

499
01:02:55,880 --> 01:03:01,660
He was one of the doors
opening to Jannah(heaven).

500
01:03:07,375 --> 01:03:16,925
But Yahuda, one of his closest followers,
betrayed Jesus...

501
01:03:20,629 --> 01:03:27,809
Yahuda's betrayal against Jesus was
for a bit of wealth.

502
01:03:29,994 --> 01:03:37,904
He was a slave of his desires to
sell Jannah (heaven) for a handful of gold.

503
01:03:41,697 --> 01:03:45,307
But, Cenab-i Haqq (Allah)...

504
01:03:46,000 --> 01:03:50,580
made Yahuda hoisted by his
own petard.

505
01:03:55,013 --> 01:03:57,593
What does Nisa Surah say?

506
01:03:59,496 --> 01:04:04,456
With Allah's power,
A stranger was shown as Jesus to them...

507
01:04:04,859 --> 01:04:11,269
They thought he was Jesus, and stretched
him on the crucifix.

508
01:04:14,771 --> 01:04:19,601
Allah raised Jesus to His place
before...

509
01:04:19,621 --> 01:04:22,871
they stretched Jesus on the crucifix.

510
01:04:23,669 --> 01:04:30,673
So, they neither killed Jesus,
nor killed him.

511
01:04:33,860 --> 01:04:40,390
However, the one they killed was shown
to them as Jesus.

512
01:04:42,283 --> 01:04:47,393
You are right that Yahuda betrayed
holy Jesus.

513
01:04:47,915 --> 01:04:54,715
But you are in a great delusion to think
that someone else was sacrificed.

514
01:06:13,844 --> 01:06:17,894
- I saw a herd of pigs.
- Did you hunt them?

515
01:06:21,874 --> 01:06:23,224
Be quiet!

516
01:06:25,492 --> 01:06:27,222
Idiots!

517
01:06:28,063 --> 01:06:29,733
Stay here.

518
01:08:13,703 --> 01:08:16,252
That direction!
Come with me.

519
01:08:18,913 --> 01:08:20,314
Let's go.

520
01:08:24,529 --> 01:08:28,078
I am not in a delusion because those
are not my words.

521
01:08:28,912 --> 01:08:34,603
If you want to argue, I won't refuse you,
Priest Efendi.

522
01:08:44,836 --> 01:08:46,966
My Sheik, excuse me.

523
01:08:47,698 --> 01:08:51,358
I want to talk to Priest Gregor
on an important subject.

524
01:09:13,506 --> 01:09:15,957
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.
(in the name of God, the merciful and compassionate.)

525
01:09:23,731 --> 01:09:26,401
Tell me, Bahadir Alp.

526
01:09:28,033 --> 01:09:35,233
You must have seen more Alps
compared to a Dervish.

527
01:09:36,904 --> 01:09:40,944
Are you a loyal Alp to your Osman Bey...

528
01:09:42,770 --> 01:09:46,071
like Pahlivan Dervish being loyal
to his Dervish?

529
01:09:49,550 --> 01:09:55,430
Pahlivan Dervish is just as loyal as
any Kayi Alp.

530
01:09:56,052 --> 01:09:57,992
Sheik Efendi.

531
01:09:58,599 --> 01:10:00,379
Eyvallah (okay).

532
01:10:16,723 --> 01:10:19,363
You recovered fast, Priest.

533
01:10:20,033 --> 01:10:22,753
You look good.

534
01:10:23,252 --> 01:10:24,942
Thank you. Yes, I'm fine.

535
01:10:29,286 --> 01:10:31,036
Priest.

536
01:10:32,367 --> 01:10:36,207
I know very well what this
mysterious relic is.

537
01:10:42,519 --> 01:10:45,679
Since this shroud is more precious
than your life...

538
01:10:47,770 --> 01:10:52,400
then it is our duty to preserve
it properly.

539
01:10:52,703 --> 01:10:54,603
Do not worry.

540
01:11:00,388 --> 01:11:02,808
First of all, I want you to know that.

541
01:11:04,835 --> 01:11:08,355
I want to talk to you about another issue.

542
01:11:10,168 --> 01:11:12,768
I want you to go somewhere.

543
01:11:13,445 --> 01:11:15,955
Can you talk to me clearly, Osman Bey?

544
01:11:17,058 --> 01:11:19,778
A village that is near to Kestel.

545
01:11:21,635 --> 01:11:23,765
It is in the borders of İnegöl
feudal lands.

546
01:11:23,966 --> 01:11:26,366
Everyone in the village is
Orthodox Christian.

547
01:11:28,174 --> 01:11:32,734
But their situation is worse than ever.

548
01:11:34,416 --> 01:11:37,856
They take all their assets under
the name of tax.

549
01:11:38,299 --> 01:11:42,629
They even torture those who
want to oppose it.

550
01:11:45,561 --> 01:11:50,761
I want you to salve these
oppressed co-religionists of yours.

551
01:11:51,961 --> 01:11:54,631
How can I be helpful to them?

552
01:11:55,140 --> 01:11:57,161
I couldn't even protect myself, Osman
Bey.

553
01:11:57,161 --> 01:11:59,851
Haven't I told you just before, Priest?

554
01:12:00,050 --> 01:12:02,690
Your life and your holy relic
are under our protection.

555
01:12:03,819 --> 01:12:07,469
Do you think I will send you there alone?

556
01:12:08,591 --> 01:12:13,731
Do not worry.
My soldiers will be with you too.

557
01:12:16,360 --> 01:12:18,910
They will protect you, do not worry.

558
01:12:19,192 --> 01:12:26,582
I want your existence and your words
to be a savior for the oppressed in there.

559
01:12:27,745 --> 01:12:30,185
What do you want me to tell them?

560
01:12:31,039 --> 01:12:32,809
The truth.

561
01:12:33,619 --> 01:12:35,809
The truth, Priest.

562
01:12:36,585 --> 01:12:40,075
I want you to tell them what you've been
through since you came to Söğüt.

563
01:12:42,387 --> 01:12:46,797
I want them to know that the
truth will always defeat oppression.

564
01:12:48,876 --> 01:12:51,346
I believe in your sincerity, Osman Bey.

565
01:12:51,788 --> 01:12:53,348
I will go to that village.

566
01:12:54,731 --> 01:12:57,771
Let's start preparations as soon
as possible.

567
01:13:53,885 --> 01:13:55,395
Turgut Bey.

568
01:13:57,593 --> 01:13:59,273
The poison needs to be removed.

569
01:14:13,219 --> 01:14:14,739
Hold on.

570
01:14:15,415 --> 01:14:16,975
Be a little patient.

571
01:14:19,806 --> 01:14:21,376
Hold on.

572
01:15:43,651 --> 01:15:45,461
Are you feeling better?

573
01:15:46,565 --> 01:15:48,015
Yes.

574
01:15:54,152 --> 01:15:57,432
But whenever I see a snake,
I see you.

575
01:15:57,944 --> 01:16:01,314
You have no idea that you are in the
den of the snakes.

576
01:16:06,209 --> 01:16:08,019
Easy, easy.

577
01:16:13,314 --> 01:16:14,954
Cornelia!

578
01:16:17,629 --> 01:16:19,067
Cornelia!

579
01:16:19,067 --> 01:16:20,877
Come here.

580
01:16:24,201 --> 01:16:27,951
You owe me another life, Miss Byzantium.

581
01:16:28,267 --> 01:16:31,667
I don't like to be in debt to anyone. We
will be even.

582
01:16:41,057 --> 01:16:42,647
Are you okay, Miss?

583
01:16:42,851 --> 01:16:44,321
I'm okay.

584
01:16:46,035 --> 01:16:47,795
Don't do anything.

585
01:16:48,960 --> 01:16:50,310
Don't do anything.

586
01:16:59,191 --> 01:17:01,891
Soldiers! Bring the horses here.

587
01:17:21,256 --> 01:17:23,616
What did he tell you?

588
01:17:34,891 --> 01:17:40,471
Osman knows that the holy relic is the
cross on which Jesus Christ was crucified.

589
01:17:41,909 --> 01:17:45,179
A piece of the cross on which
Jesus was crucified.

590
01:17:55,629 --> 01:17:58,279
He will never give it to us.

591
01:17:59,186 --> 01:18:03,406
We will go to a village near Kastelion
by the will and protection of Osman.

592
01:18:04,202 --> 01:18:07,922
The villagers are all Orthodox Christians.

593
01:18:08,451 --> 01:18:10,901
Are we going to act on Osman's word?

594
01:18:11,968 --> 01:18:13,908
You have just recovered.

595
01:18:27,473 --> 01:18:29,173
She is here.

596
01:18:34,183 --> 01:18:35,693
I hope nothing's wrong.

597
01:18:46,947 --> 01:18:48,697
Aygül Hatun.

598
01:18:49,422 --> 01:18:51,182
Cerkutay.

599
01:18:58,082 --> 01:18:59,782
Say what you need to.

600
01:19:00,943 --> 01:19:03,243
Do you remember the flower...

601
01:19:03,243 --> 01:19:05,405
I gave you yesterday?

602
01:19:06,232 --> 01:19:08,182
Its name is the flower of the mystery.

603
01:19:11,824 --> 01:19:16,664
Whoever gives that flower to someone...

604
01:19:19,542 --> 01:19:22,202
has to reveal his secret to that person.

605
01:19:23,724 --> 01:19:25,984
I will tell you my secret.

606
01:19:30,380 --> 01:19:32,600
I'm in love with you.

607
01:19:54,916 --> 01:19:58,636
This secret is too much for both of us,
Cerkutay.

608
01:20:23,086 --> 01:20:24,646
Cerkutay.

609
01:20:25,977 --> 01:20:28,397
You revealed your secret, Cerkutay.

610
01:20:30,024 --> 01:20:32,644
Brave Cerkutay.

611
01:20:33,654 --> 01:20:36,084
Did you think loving someone is easy?

612
01:20:36,328 --> 01:20:38,698
It's easy to endure its pleasure...

613
01:20:39,906 --> 01:20:43,136
but when you endure the suffering of it,
it becomes love.

614
01:20:45,185 --> 01:20:47,405
This is love, Cerkutay!

615
01:20:47,845 --> 01:20:53,865
It enslaves even the sultans and
burns the lovers to ashes.

616
01:21:00,334 --> 01:21:02,284
Don't give up on love.

617
01:21:05,510 --> 01:21:10,650
You have to endure both the curse and
the bless.

618
01:21:17,667 --> 01:21:20,167
Don't turn your back on love.

619
01:21:20,502 --> 01:21:22,802
Love can't be turned away.

620
01:21:31,612 --> 01:21:34,022
Burn, Cerkutay. Burn.

621
01:21:51,967 --> 01:21:55,327
Inegol Frontier Village
Nearby Kastellion

622
01:22:02,252 --> 01:22:05,502
It's him. The Priest!

623
01:22:06,204 --> 01:22:08,434
He is coming!

624
01:22:10,710 --> 01:22:13,770
Welcome, Priest.

625
01:22:17,086 --> 01:22:20,186
Welcome.

626
01:22:48,001 --> 01:22:50,451
Jesus Christ bliss you...

627
01:22:50,517 --> 01:22:52,437
and forgive your sins.

628
01:22:53,041 --> 01:22:57,881
I had many other things on my mind when
I was coming from Constantinople...

629
01:22:58,217 --> 01:23:02,587
or rather, when I was escaping from
the Emperor's tyranny.

630
01:23:03,307 --> 01:23:09,487
But as some of you have heard, God
crossed my path with Osman Bey.

631
01:23:10,126 --> 01:23:14,985
Why did you stay in a Turk plain
instead of a feudal land, Priest?

632
01:23:14,985 --> 01:23:18,137
Why didn't you go to the Lord Nicolo?
He would protect you.

633
01:23:18,137 --> 01:23:20,847
He gives great value to the nobility.

634
01:23:23,245 --> 01:23:26,135
May Jesus Christ's love be with you.

635
01:23:26,492 --> 01:23:29,062
You are a very kind-hearted person.

636
01:23:29,311 --> 01:23:32,478
But Nicolo wouldn't have done that.

637
01:23:32,478 --> 01:23:37,538
For the power he wanted to gain, he would
leave me alone with the Emperor's tyranny.

638
01:23:39,894 --> 01:23:44,374
You didn't go to the Lord Kosses too
because he is close to the Emperor.

639
01:23:44,890 --> 01:23:48,020
We understand this. But why didn't you go
to the Lord Rogatus?

640
01:23:48,037 --> 01:23:51,377
We heard that he is close to you.
He would protect you.

641
01:23:51,992 --> 01:23:53,272
That's true.

642
01:23:54,047 --> 01:23:55,889
I thought so too.

643
01:23:55,889 --> 01:24:01,739
But Rogatus acted like the others
when it came to gaining power.

644
01:24:01,922 --> 01:24:04,222
He left me stranded.

645
01:24:04,330 --> 01:24:08,120
But Osman Bey kept me safe.

646
01:24:11,900 --> 01:24:16,720
Moreover, when I saw the Christian
people and the church...

647
01:24:16,720 --> 01:24:20,090
in Söğüt, I realized that this attitude
was not special to me.

648
01:24:20,099 --> 01:24:24,949
I have never seen such justice
and mercy in any feudal land...

649
01:24:25,011 --> 01:24:28,721
even though we are co-religionists.

650
01:24:33,548 --> 01:24:35,868
I heard about the church in the village.

651
01:24:36,294 --> 01:24:40,274
Each of them persecutes their
people for their personal gain.

652
01:24:40,859 --> 01:24:45,169
They ignore people's most basic needs.

653
01:24:45,732 --> 01:24:47,793
I heard about the church in this village.

654
01:24:47,793 --> 01:24:51,853
Doesn't this state of the church
break your heart?

655
01:24:52,125 --> 01:24:54,625
They do not meet the needs of
our church at all.

656
01:24:55,477 --> 01:24:57,558
It is like a barn.

657
01:24:57,558 --> 01:25:03,298
Osman Bey keeps the church in Söğüt
well-kept as if it were his own temple.

658
01:25:03,383 --> 01:25:09,523
He governs the Christians fairly without
discriminating them from the Muslims.

659
01:25:09,871 --> 01:25:14,601
I have a relative who lives in Söğüt.
It's true. They are very satisfied.

660
01:25:14,619 --> 01:25:17,879
I heard that they don't pay
high taxes as we do.

661
01:25:18,518 --> 01:25:21,118
They do not interfere with
their religion too.

662
01:25:28,374 --> 01:25:30,644
We couldn't satisfy the
Lords for years.

663
01:25:40,122 --> 01:25:41,802
Inegol Castle.

664
01:25:47,576 --> 01:25:51,906
Priest Gregor came to your village and
gave a speech that praises Osman Bey.

665
01:25:52,392 --> 01:25:55,452
Your people were greatly
affected by this speech.

666
01:26:00,141 --> 01:26:01,801
Argos.

667
01:26:18,478 --> 01:26:22,658
It seems that Osman learned where
the caravan is.

668
01:26:25,073 --> 01:26:27,893
That's why he sent the Priest for the
speech.

669
01:26:28,863 --> 01:26:32,017
The Priest is still in the village.

670
01:26:32,017 --> 01:26:34,247
I think we can get him.

671
01:26:36,165 --> 01:26:38,367
We have nothing to do with
the Priest anymore.

672
01:26:38,367 --> 01:26:41,648
There is something more important.

673
01:26:41,648 --> 01:26:43,998
But Osman has it.

674
01:26:44,847 --> 01:26:49,777
Otherwise, Osman wouldn't send the Priest
that easy and without protection.

675
01:26:52,574 --> 01:26:55,984
Position your soldiers
well in the village, Argus.

676
01:26:59,624 --> 01:27:02,764
Osman knows that the caravan
will come to the village.

677
01:27:04,087 --> 01:27:09,547
But he doesn't know that we know this.

678
01:27:12,812 --> 01:27:15,532
I will prepare a big surprise for him.

679
01:27:17,449 --> 01:27:19,229
A very big surprise.

680
01:27:27,584 --> 01:27:31,464
Harmankaya Castle.

681
01:27:32,443 --> 01:27:38,123
I heard what you wanted me to learn while
the Priest was talking to someone else.

682
01:27:39,520 --> 01:27:41,850
It is a piece of the cross.

683
01:27:44,915 --> 01:27:48,785
It is said that the piece is from the
cross that Jesus Christ was crucified.

684
01:27:48,998 --> 01:27:50,398
What?

685
01:27:51,922 --> 01:27:54,652
The cross on which Jesus Christ
was crucified.

686
01:27:57,336 --> 01:28:00,866
Do you realize what you are saying,
Bahadır?

687
01:28:02,462 --> 01:28:04,362
Yes. They are saying it's true.

688
01:28:04,549 --> 01:28:07,249
Are you sure that it is the
cross of Jesus Christ?

689
01:28:07,424 --> 01:28:10,714
Yes, Lord Kosses. I'm sure.

690
01:28:20,968 --> 01:28:22,438
Bahadır.

691
01:28:22,840 --> 01:28:27,420
You can't even imagine the importance
of this information that you brought.

692
01:28:38,773 --> 01:28:42,063
These golds are for the information.

693
01:28:43,403 --> 01:28:47,423
Think what you can get...

694
01:28:50,489 --> 01:28:53,949
If you can bring me the relic
you speak of.

695
01:28:56,818 --> 01:28:58,738
I will do it, Lord Kosses.

696
01:29:00,257 --> 01:29:02,247
You will do it.

697
01:29:04,290 --> 01:29:06,230
And don't you dare to forget...

698
01:29:07,236 --> 01:29:08,556
Bahadır.

699
01:29:09,125 --> 01:29:11,545
Punishment and reward are twins.

700
01:29:12,191 --> 01:29:14,721
Don't you dare to return empty-handed.

701
01:29:24,387 --> 01:29:26,507
Look at this, Maria.

702
01:29:26,775 --> 01:29:28,815
Look at Osman Bey.

703
01:29:28,815 --> 01:29:31,398
He holds the heart of the Christian world
in his hands.

704
01:29:31,398 --> 01:29:35,098
But that heart should be in the hands
of the one who deserves it, brother.

705
01:29:36,380 --> 01:29:37,540
Yes.

706
01:29:38,310 --> 01:29:40,870
If we can get the relic, Maria...

707
01:29:41,339 --> 01:29:45,999
not also Bithynia but the whole of Rome
will be down on its knees.

708
01:29:53,289 --> 01:29:55,339
Thank you, Malhun Hatun.

709
01:29:55,857 --> 01:30:00,407
She returned with an intelligence that
would make us victorious.

710
01:30:03,793 --> 01:30:06,533
A caravan departed from Damascus.

711
01:30:07,685 --> 01:30:13,404
According to the information we got,
the belongings of Kosses, Nicolo...

712
01:30:13,404 --> 01:30:16,394
and even Rogatus are in that caravan.

713
01:30:17,413 --> 01:30:20,143
Ten times more than what we got before.

714
01:30:25,165 --> 01:30:29,945
Silk, spices, and all kinds of jewelry.

715
01:30:30,944 --> 01:30:33,214
It is full of heavy goods.

716
01:30:37,590 --> 01:30:41,240
The destination of this caravan is
Kastelion.

717
01:30:42,759 --> 01:30:45,969
A village near the castle we call Kestel.

718
01:30:47,969 --> 01:30:53,369
My Bey, it is possible to get there
without stepping our land.

719
01:30:53,910 --> 01:30:56,200
It is their land for now, Demirci.

720
01:30:57,661 --> 01:31:03,481
But before the caravan comes, that village
will be under our control.

721
01:31:04,700 --> 01:31:07,010
Inshallah.

722
01:31:07,097 --> 01:31:08,667
My Bey.

723
01:31:09,236 --> 01:31:11,396
This is a cause of war.

724
01:31:12,924 --> 01:31:15,084
You are talking about getting land.

725
01:31:15,346 --> 01:31:19,526
Lord and even the
Emperors will be after us.

726
01:31:20,222 --> 01:31:23,092
We've been at war since
the day we got the Priest.

727
01:31:23,766 --> 01:31:26,316
It's not the time to pray.

728
01:31:27,016 --> 01:31:29,816
Everyone will act according to
their nature.

729
01:31:29,990 --> 01:31:34,800
They will go into their holes like
snakes and we will fight like wolves.

730
01:31:38,709 --> 01:31:40,843
Let the preparations be made
until tomorrow.

731
01:31:40,843 --> 01:31:42,903
Now is the time of the conquest.

732
01:31:44,119 --> 01:31:45,969
As you ordered, my Bey.

733
01:31:46,218 --> 01:31:48,018
As you ordered, my Bey.

734
01:31:49,008 --> 01:31:50,468
Yes, my Bey.

735
01:31:58,581 --> 01:32:02,881
If you allow, I want to be a part of this
bright conquest, my Bey.

736
01:32:10,796 --> 01:32:15,566
When there are so many soldiers waiting
to be martyred, is this the right time?

737
01:32:16,700 --> 01:32:18,740
If you come, what will Orhan do?

738
01:32:26,075 --> 01:32:29,975
He doesn't have only one mother, my
Bey. Orhan is our Orhan.

739
01:32:31,809 --> 01:32:33,529
Bala is his mother too.

740
01:32:34,790 --> 01:32:39,510
Until I come back, his other mother can
look after him, can't you, Bala Hatun?

741
01:32:46,872 --> 01:32:48,482
Of course.

742
01:32:48,707 --> 01:32:50,547
Of course, I will look after my Orhan.

743
01:32:55,172 --> 01:32:58,792
Malhun Hatun has longed for war
for a long time, my Bey.

744
01:33:01,196 --> 01:33:02,956
Thank you, Bala Hatun.

745
01:33:03,156 --> 01:33:04,686
Thank you.

746
01:33:06,921 --> 01:33:11,271
If so, get ready, Malhun.

747
01:33:13,015 --> 01:33:15,745
Then it's time to sharpen the weapons,
my Bey.

748
01:33:16,831 --> 01:33:18,391
I will go to Davut Usta.

749
01:33:18,479 --> 01:33:20,239
Excuse me.

750
01:33:33,623 --> 01:33:35,613
Thank you.

751
01:33:36,440 --> 01:33:38,910
-Thank you, Gonca.
-Enjoy.

752
01:33:41,274 --> 01:33:43,964
-Thank you, my Hatun.
-Enjoy.

753
01:33:50,312 --> 01:33:54,132
Here you go, let's eat.

754
01:33:54,785 --> 01:33:56,685
In the name of Allah.

755
01:33:57,178 --> 01:33:58,698
Enjoy your meal.

756
01:34:42,882 --> 01:34:45,372
Why are you not eating?

757
01:34:52,710 --> 01:34:54,580
What's wrong with you?

758
01:34:55,789 --> 01:34:57,809
You are Osman Bey's head Alp.

759
01:35:03,882 --> 01:35:05,342
Göktuğ.

760
01:35:05,714 --> 01:35:08,634
You can't be in a bad mood.

761
01:35:09,342 --> 01:35:11,792
Even though I disappointed my Bey?

762
01:35:11,792 --> 01:35:14,712
You are thinking only about yourself.

763
01:35:15,028 --> 01:35:18,488
While our Bey is saying to be together,
you are being selfish. Don't.

764
01:35:18,912 --> 01:35:23,322
Because Turgut Bey brought their
carcasses, you are languishing.

765
01:35:23,488 --> 01:35:27,368
I'm not being selfish, Boran. Turgut
Bey is the one who is being selfish.

766
01:35:27,617 --> 01:35:31,682
You saw how he bragged.

767
01:35:31,682 --> 01:35:34,442
People see what they want to see.

768
01:35:35,989 --> 01:35:38,839
Our Bey's ambition is to unite
all the Turks.

769
01:35:40,425 --> 01:35:43,695
Instead of being happy that Turgut Bey
is fighting by our side...

770
01:35:43,985 --> 01:35:46,305
you are languishing.

771
01:35:47,256 --> 01:35:51,086
Brother, the enemy is one, we are one.

772
01:35:51,459 --> 01:35:52,789
Don't do this.

773
01:35:53,505 --> 01:35:57,328
You are telling the truth. But what
bothers me is...

774
01:35:57,328 --> 01:36:01,858
Brother. What is important for Osman Bey
is important for us.

775
01:36:03,450 --> 01:36:05,430
Don't do this, Göktuğ.

776
01:36:16,503 --> 01:36:19,813
Come on. Let's eat now.

777
01:36:21,129 --> 01:36:23,069
Thank you, brother.

778
01:36:59,009 --> 01:37:01,509
-Good luck with it, Malhun Hatun.
-Thank you, Bala.

779
01:37:01,682 --> 01:37:03,446
Let me help you.

780
01:37:03,446 --> 01:37:05,086
Don't carry it.

781
01:37:14,724 --> 01:37:16,224
Alaca.

782
01:37:19,367 --> 01:37:20,627
Alaca.

783
01:37:27,587 --> 01:37:30,297
Do you want to go to the war too?

784
01:37:30,807 --> 01:37:32,967
Are you bored here too?

785
01:37:41,356 --> 01:37:43,616
Be a little patient, Alaca.

786
01:37:45,429 --> 01:37:50,159
After Bala Hatun gives birth, you can
go to any war you want.

787
01:37:52,181 --> 01:37:54,091
Inshallah.

788
01:37:58,310 --> 01:37:59,980
Malhun Hatun.

789
01:38:01,185 --> 01:38:02,585
My Orhan.

790
01:38:07,025 --> 01:38:08,865
My Orhan.

791
01:38:09,513 --> 01:38:11,443
My child.

792
01:38:13,556 --> 01:38:15,736
My brave child.

793
01:38:20,071 --> 01:38:21,851
You are cold.

794
01:38:23,534 --> 01:38:27,024
Let me take him. I will keep him
warm, do not worry.

795
01:38:28,842 --> 01:38:31,032
His mother Bala will look after my Orhan.

796
01:38:31,359 --> 01:38:33,299
I will not worry at all.

797
01:38:37,708 --> 01:38:40,728
I know that you will look after him
as he is your own child.

798
01:38:41,129 --> 01:38:42,809
Of course.

799
01:38:51,137 --> 01:38:55,717
While you are fighting with the enemy,
we will pray here.

800
01:38:56,165 --> 01:38:58,625
More power to your elbow, Malhun
Hatun.

801
01:38:58,834 --> 01:39:01,014
Thank you, Bala Hatun.

802
01:40:00,958 --> 01:40:03,138
-Cerkutay!
-My bey.

803
01:40:04,281 --> 01:40:05,661
Go now.

804
01:40:06,742 --> 01:40:08,722
But keep your eyes open.

805
01:40:09,277 --> 01:40:11,947
Let's see the situation in the village.

806
01:40:12,070 --> 01:40:14,030
Let's see what's awaiting us.

807
01:40:14,725 --> 01:40:17,235
If you allow me, my bey.

808
01:40:56,195 --> 01:40:59,095
Aren't we friends, Malhun Hatun?

809
01:41:00,213 --> 01:41:02,463
What did I do to deserve this?

810
01:41:05,410 --> 01:41:07,510
Stay calm, Gökçe girl.

811
01:41:08,947 --> 01:41:12,267
Why are you talking to yourself?

812
01:41:15,327 --> 01:41:18,366
I'm busy, Bahadır Bey.
Annoy someone else.

813
01:41:18,366 --> 01:41:20,176
Gökçe girl.

814
01:41:21,443 --> 01:41:24,073
You are from Kızılbeyoğlu Tribe.

815
01:41:24,302 --> 01:41:26,572
I know your childhood.

816
01:41:27,213 --> 01:41:29,493
You were nimble.

817
01:41:31,593 --> 01:41:34,513
It doesn't you to bow your head like this.

818
01:41:34,837 --> 01:41:36,437
Raise your head.

819
01:41:44,292 --> 01:41:45,862
Here.

820
01:41:47,353 --> 01:41:48,673
Take it.

821
01:41:56,638 --> 01:41:59,038
Don't lower your head that easily.

822
01:42:00,586 --> 01:42:02,966
Let it remind you who you are.

823
01:42:12,923 --> 01:42:15,563
Patrol there.

824
01:42:18,466 --> 01:42:20,546
And you, there.

825
01:42:23,220 --> 01:42:25,190
You, there.

826
01:42:27,525 --> 01:42:29,615
You protect the gate.

827
01:42:50,269 --> 01:42:51,779
Master Gregor.

828
01:42:52,728 --> 01:42:55,268
Your influence on the people is great.

829
01:42:55,330 --> 01:42:57,930
They were impressed by your
speech yesterday.

830
01:42:59,572 --> 01:43:02,232
But that speech will benefit Osman.

831
01:43:02,654 --> 01:43:05,604
Don't you think that you help him
too much?

832
01:43:06,481 --> 01:43:10,211
Andreas, let us be useful for Osman.

833
01:43:10,725 --> 01:43:16,085
For now, what we need is to gain Osman's
trust. I told you.

834
01:43:17,991 --> 01:43:19,771
You go this way!

835
01:43:29,226 --> 01:43:33,376
Master, the street is full of
Lord Nikola's soldiers.

836
01:43:46,360 --> 01:43:48,630
There wasn't this many yesterday.

837
01:43:50,669 --> 01:43:53,399
Maybe this is Osman's plan.

838
01:43:54,089 --> 01:43:56,049
What is Osman up to again?

839
01:43:57,035 --> 01:43:59,135
I can catch up to his intelligence.

840
01:44:12,067 --> 01:44:13,997
Mashallah!

841
01:44:14,012 --> 01:44:18,242
Malhun! You look full of life because
of the battle.

842
01:44:18,502 --> 01:44:23,392
I am! We haven't fought side by
side for too long.

843
01:44:23,991 --> 01:44:25,511
True!

844
01:44:32,161 --> 01:44:33,811
Cerkutay!

845
01:44:39,906 --> 01:44:42,964
The village is like a hell. There are
soldiers everywhere.

846
01:44:42,964 --> 01:44:46,414
What is it, Cerkutay?
Are you afraid?

847
01:44:47,970 --> 01:44:52,780
I'm Osman Bey's alp. Does fear suit
us when we are with you, my bey?

848
01:44:53,146 --> 01:44:54,106
True!

849
01:45:01,133 --> 01:45:02,993
Alps!

850
01:45:04,673 --> 01:45:08,163
They want to scotch the Kayı
and punish us!

851
01:45:10,173 --> 01:45:14,583
Those who spill blood on the bread
of my people...

852
01:45:14,583 --> 01:45:18,613
will be punished by me!

853
01:45:20,240 --> 01:45:25,750
If they scotch our trade, we scotch
their caravans!

854
01:45:28,655 --> 01:45:30,945
-Boran!
-My bey.

855
01:45:31,144 --> 01:45:33,344
Bring the reports.

856
01:45:33,728 --> 01:45:35,258
As you order, my bey.

857
01:45:49,433 --> 01:45:52,205
İnegöl Border Village
Near Kastelion

858
01:45:52,205 --> 01:45:54,015
Listen to me well now.

859
01:45:54,345 --> 01:45:56,515
It's market time in the village.

860
01:45:56,987 --> 01:45:58,797
It's full of people.

861
01:46:15,247 --> 01:46:18,077
So, you will hide well.

862
01:46:18,830 --> 01:46:21,590
There will be an alp for every
one of them.

863
01:46:46,277 --> 01:46:48,007
Cerkutay.

864
01:46:48,482 --> 01:46:50,702
You will reach the narrow street.

865
01:46:50,899 --> 01:46:53,649
You know how to hide well.

866
01:46:59,290 --> 01:47:04,470
Malhun, Aygül; you will disguise
us villager women.

867
01:47:05,316 --> 01:47:06,986
I will be there too.

868
01:47:07,368 --> 01:47:08,908
With my alps.

869
01:47:10,110 --> 01:47:12,700
We'll strike down the patrolling
soldiers first.

870
01:47:19,993 --> 01:47:24,773
With many tricks and traps,
no one will leave any mark behind.

871
01:48:00,782 --> 01:48:03,252
They will be hanged.

872
01:48:31,334 --> 01:48:35,914
The most important thing is, you will
look out for each other.

873
01:49:33,107 --> 01:49:35,017
Soldiers!

874
01:50:00,666 --> 01:50:02,766
My God, protect us.

875
01:50:19,313 --> 01:50:21,263
The arrow came this way!

876
01:50:21,664 --> 01:50:23,834
Run! Run!

877
01:51:45,025 --> 01:51:46,955
Where are they?

878
01:51:48,684 --> 01:51:49,924
Where are they?

879
01:52:33,274 --> 01:52:35,454
Allah is eternal!

880
01:53:22,664 --> 01:53:24,574
Come on, Andreas.

881
01:53:39,520 --> 01:53:41,160
Alps!

882
01:53:57,871 --> 01:53:59,431
Alps!

883
01:54:00,611 --> 01:54:02,771
Gather the people in the center.

884
01:54:02,861 --> 01:54:05,041
As you order my bey!

885
01:54:18,641 --> 01:54:22,591
Now I understand why you sent
me here, Osman Bey.

886
01:54:24,013 --> 01:54:26,923
It's good that you do, Priest Gregor.

887
01:54:29,293 --> 01:54:32,053
This is the only thing I want to see.

888
01:54:32,501 --> 01:54:35,801
For the Christian people to catch
their breath under the flag of Kayı.

889
01:54:38,375 --> 01:54:39,795
Come on.

890
01:56:28,069 --> 01:56:33,349
What is it, Argus?
Are you afraid of Osman?

891
01:56:34,239 --> 01:56:35,439
Sir.

892
01:56:36,137 --> 01:56:39,407
-You said they might be in the village.
-And?

893
01:56:39,908 --> 01:56:43,068
We put many soldiers in the village.

894
01:56:43,489 --> 01:56:45,249
Isn't that so?

895
01:56:45,416 --> 01:56:46,901
Yes, sir.

896
01:56:47,091 --> 01:56:51,801
Then, there is no need for fear.

897
01:56:52,883 --> 01:56:56,453
I don't like cowards.

898
01:57:00,208 --> 01:57:02,898
If Osman is expecting us in the village.

899
01:57:02,909 --> 01:57:08,359
Let us wait a little longer to
make him more impatient.

900
01:57:09,774 --> 01:57:11,334
More.

901
01:57:39,873 --> 01:57:44,273
I am Ertuğrul Ghazi's son, Osman Bey!

902
01:57:45,110 --> 01:57:47,110
The bey of the Kayı!

903
01:57:48,190 --> 01:57:50,270
I'm known by some of you.

904
01:57:51,854 --> 01:57:55,204
The rest will start from now.

905
01:57:57,190 --> 01:58:00,230
We don't plunder the lands
we conquer.

906
01:58:00,636 --> 01:58:02,586
We revive them.

907
01:58:02,822 --> 01:58:04,552
We make them home.

908
01:58:06,426 --> 01:58:12,716
And we know that those who rule with
tyranny will go to hell.

909
01:58:16,983 --> 01:58:21,223
For this reason, we are only afraid
of Allah!

910
01:58:22,475 --> 01:58:25,815
Our laws are his laws.

911
01:58:32,908 --> 01:58:34,848
And from now...

912
01:58:35,827 --> 01:58:38,777
your property, your lives...

913
01:58:39,305 --> 01:58:43,195
and your faith is protected by me!

914
01:58:49,773 --> 01:58:52,153
Your taxes are in half.

915
01:58:55,755 --> 01:58:57,565
Stay in ease.

916
01:59:08,843 --> 01:59:10,493
People!

917
01:59:10,827 --> 01:59:13,549
I've lived with Osman Bey for a while.

918
01:59:13,549 --> 01:59:18,609
As I told him that he can't keep me a
captive, he would say that I'm a guest.

919
01:59:19,611 --> 01:59:24,741
In the meantime, I saw that there is
no captivity under Osman Bey's banner.

920
01:59:25,393 --> 01:59:29,323
There is only freedom, justice,
and mercy.

921
01:59:43,625 --> 01:59:46,195
If you have something to say,
say it now.

922
01:59:46,324 --> 01:59:49,634
And those who feel content go
to their home now.

923
01:59:52,865 --> 01:59:54,935
May God protect you, Osman Bey.

924
01:59:58,785 --> 02:00:03,495
We stand with whoever Priest Gregor
stands with.

925
02:00:04,442 --> 02:00:08,582
Thank you. What good did the lord
do for us anyway?

926
02:00:23,212 --> 02:00:27,052
My bey, the caravan
is near.

927
02:00:32,671 --> 02:00:34,551
Let them come.

928
02:00:35,618 --> 02:00:37,328
Let them come.

929
02:01:05,992 --> 02:01:17,868
Long live Osman Bey!

930
02:01:18,318 --> 02:01:21,858
Mashallah!

931
02:01:22,995 --> 02:01:25,005
The valiants of the Kayı...

932
02:01:25,457 --> 02:01:27,877
are idolizing Osman Bey!

933
02:01:29,402 --> 02:01:33,152
Do you know who Osman Bey
idolizes?

934
02:01:33,752 --> 02:01:35,952
Who is it?

935
02:01:36,255 --> 02:01:37,825
Shah-ı Mardan.

936
02:01:38,985 --> 02:01:41,105
The shah of the braves.

937
02:01:41,767 --> 02:01:44,537
He idolizes Hz.Ali.

938
02:01:45,989 --> 02:01:50,969
Hz.Ali's courage knows no limits!

939
02:01:51,932 --> 02:01:54,112
He jumps on his white horse
and comes.

940
02:01:54,565 --> 02:01:58,135
He takes us to Mecca.

941
02:02:02,483 --> 02:02:05,413
-Should he take you to Mecca?
-Yes!

942
02:02:05,675 --> 02:02:08,605
Yes! Yes!

943
02:02:11,284 --> 02:02:16,064
Our dear prophet's army sieged
Hayber.

944
02:02:16,724 --> 02:02:19,974
The siege lasted 20 whole days.

945
02:02:20,630 --> 02:02:23,350
The number of martyrs
increased every day.

946
02:02:24,611 --> 02:02:28,301
There were more than 2000 martyrs
and more than 5000 wounded.

947
02:02:31,770 --> 02:02:36,400
But there is no yielding!
Does it suit a Muslim to give up?

948
02:02:36,546 --> 02:02:39,806
It doesn't!

949
02:02:42,107 --> 02:02:45,917
Great commanders stood on the gates
of Hayber Castle.

950
02:02:46,747 --> 02:02:48,617
But no one can open it!

951
02:02:49,333 --> 02:02:54,123
Our dear prophet took his black banner
on his holy hand.

952
02:02:54,725 --> 02:02:58,265
He told Selman-ı Talisi to
call Ali.

953
02:02:59,871 --> 02:03:01,211
Selman was surprised.

954
02:03:02,170 --> 02:03:07,970
Hz.Ali was next to our holy prophet
with his sick eyes.

955
02:03:10,112 --> 02:03:17,062
Our dear prophet prays for Ali's
sick eyes to heal.

956
02:03:19,896 --> 02:03:23,763
He gives him the black flag.

957
02:03:23,763 --> 02:03:29,473
And say that the conquest of Hayber
will happen with you.

958
02:03:33,253 --> 02:03:35,133
Can he stop?

959
02:03:35,602 --> 02:03:40,622
It's the holy prophet's words.
Hz.Ali didn't even wait for the soldiers!

960
02:03:40,974 --> 02:03:44,320
He took the banner and Zülfikar.

961
02:03:44,320 --> 02:03:47,960
And he ran to the hell-like battlefield!

962
02:03:49,065 --> 02:03:55,005
Allah Allah!
Allah Allah!

963
02:03:55,844 --> 02:03:58,934
Alarm in Hayber and curiosity
among the Jews!

964
02:04:01,204 --> 02:04:05,164
Who is this man running at our
army on his own?

965
02:04:05,705 --> 02:04:09,115
So, who are you, they said.

966
02:04:10,117 --> 02:04:12,407
Our minister Ali replied...

967
02:04:15,999 --> 02:04:19,359
I am Shah-ı Mardan.

968
02:04:20,748 --> 02:04:24,588
Soldier of the battlefield,
the Lion of Allah...

969
02:04:24,996 --> 02:04:27,506
Abu Talib's son, Ali!

970
02:04:28,622 --> 02:04:32,182
The Jews shouted in confusion!

971
02:04:33,552 --> 02:04:36,262
So, you are the one they
call Ali?

972
02:04:40,581 --> 02:04:42,561
I am the one they call Ali.

973
02:04:43,253 --> 02:04:48,733
The sword I'm wielding is called Zülfikar!

974
02:04:49,759 --> 02:04:52,509
It doesn't let the heathens rest.

975
02:04:53,194 --> 02:04:59,294
The arm that's wielding it has never been
beaten by anyone before!

976
02:05:06,903 --> 02:05:11,343
The heathens said,
why should we be afraid of you?

977
02:05:12,390 --> 02:05:18,470
You are a human just like us.
Made of bones and flesh.

978
02:05:18,913 --> 02:05:23,693
Shah-ı Mardan Ali said...

979
02:05:24,471 --> 02:05:26,401
yes, true.

980
02:05:27,580 --> 02:05:31,800
I'm a human, made of bones and flesh,
just like you.

981
02:05:32,613 --> 02:05:35,893
But I have such a power that...

982
02:05:38,213 --> 02:05:41,043
gives me the confidence I need.

983
02:05:42,538 --> 02:05:47,348
Allah Allah!
Allah Allah!

984
02:05:48,658 --> 02:05:51,128
Hz.Ali takes the banner in his hand!

985
02:05:51,612 --> 02:05:53,542
He rides his horse to the ditch!

986
02:05:54,437 --> 02:05:58,847
He passes that great ditch as if
he is a bird!

987
02:05:59,682 --> 02:06:03,052
He gets to the Hayber gates that
no one can pass!

988
02:06:04,450 --> 02:06:09,000
He holds the gate latches tightly...

989
02:06:09,104 --> 02:06:12,174
with his strong arms...

990
02:06:12,389 --> 02:06:16,579
and pull them so hard that...

991
02:06:16,852 --> 02:06:19,852
he pulls them so had that...

992
02:06:20,431 --> 02:06:24,231
finally, the gate is broken!

993
02:06:27,911 --> 02:06:33,361
There, the gate of Hayber gets
open for the Muslims.

994
02:06:34,353 --> 02:06:37,733
Where does Hz.Ali's power comes from?

995
02:06:41,596 --> 02:06:44,966
It's his faith, Ahmed.
It's his faith.

996
02:06:46,875 --> 02:06:49,165
To make the heathens kneel...

997
02:06:50,502 --> 02:06:53,482
before the power on your arms...

998
02:06:54,500 --> 02:06:56,640
you need the power
of faith.

999
02:06:57,212 --> 02:06:58,652
to be an alp!

1000
02:06:59,266 --> 02:07:05,186
A lion's heart, a steel arm and faith,
and the prophet's principles are needed.

1001
02:07:05,365 --> 02:07:07,965
Like Osman Bey, right?

1002
02:07:10,832 --> 02:07:12,922
Like Osman Bey, yes.

1003
02:07:16,223 --> 02:07:21,483
Osman Bey is like a Zülfikar
pointing the sun.

1004
02:07:22,124 --> 02:07:24,944
The oppressed take shelter
under its shadow.

1005
02:07:26,773 --> 02:07:31,333
The heathens are shattering away!

1006
02:07:32,459 --> 02:07:34,529
Mashallah!

1007
02:07:39,258 --> 02:07:41,728
Mashallah!

1008
02:07:43,165 --> 02:07:45,165
Mashallah!

1009
02:07:54,902 --> 02:07:56,872
Mashallah!

1010
02:09:01,651 --> 02:09:03,291
Nikola!

1011
02:09:10,813 --> 02:09:12,753
Welcome to Kayı lands!

1012
02:09:20,456 --> 02:09:22,336
We were expecting you.

1013
02:09:25,198 --> 02:09:27,848
Oh, Osman Bey.

1014
02:09:27,903 --> 02:09:31,003
I never thought you would be here!

1015
02:09:31,683 --> 02:09:35,623
This is our land and the caravan
is our caravan now.

1016
02:09:36,693 --> 02:09:38,503
Is that what you say?

1017
02:09:38,813 --> 02:09:42,963
Do you think you can take this village by
killing my soldiers?

1018
02:09:46,159 --> 02:09:49,919
This is my village and this
is my caravan.

1019
02:09:50,245 --> 02:09:52,685
Don't be so sure!

1020
02:11:11,126 --> 02:11:13,206
We came as you wanted, Nikola.

1021
02:11:14,059 --> 02:11:17,019
Let's not keep Osman waiting.

1022
02:11:41,938 --> 02:11:44,148
As you see, Osman Bey.

1023
02:11:44,430 --> 02:11:49,820
It's still my village and it's
still my caravan.

1024
02:11:52,359 --> 02:11:56,129
I know you well enough to not
fall into your traps.

1025
02:12:05,546 --> 02:12:07,206
Nikola!

1026
02:12:28,782 --> 02:12:30,532
Do you know me too?

1027
02:12:31,165 --> 02:12:33,305
Do you know Turgut Bey too?

1028
02:12:34,239 --> 02:12:37,139
Even if you don't, you will now.

1029
02:12:40,710 --> 02:12:45,170
The caravan is important. Its sound
will echo in the whole of Bhytinia.

1030
02:12:45,999 --> 02:12:51,669
I sent the priest. Nikola must've
taken his precautions.

1031
02:12:53,304 --> 02:12:55,704
The weasels move in packs.

1032
02:12:55,910 --> 02:12:57,890
We shouldn't be alone.

1033
02:12:58,300 --> 02:13:00,030
Stand with us.

1034
02:13:01,299 --> 02:13:04,179
It's time to have some time
with Nikola.

1035
02:13:04,726 --> 02:13:08,889
I'll be there with my alps.
The wolf survived the winter...

1036
02:13:08,889 --> 02:13:11,689
but he won't forget the
cold he endured.

1037
02:13:12,470 --> 02:13:15,080
It's time for revenge, Osman Bey.

1038
02:13:18,608 --> 02:13:20,331
Charge!

1039
02:13:20,331 --> 02:13:22,121
Ya Allah!

1040
02:14:11,839 --> 02:14:15,179
Anselmo fights for gold but doesn't
die for gold.

1041
02:14:15,609 --> 02:14:18,379
Catalonians! We are retreating!

1042
02:14:31,075 --> 02:14:33,993
-We need to leave!
-Osman!

1043
02:14:33,993 --> 02:14:36,903
-We must leave, sir!
-Wait!

1044
02:14:37,020 --> 02:14:39,940
Stop!

1045
02:15:11,836 --> 02:15:16,336
How are we any different than
Judas who betrayed Jesus?

1046
02:15:17,685 --> 02:15:21,045
We left Christian lands to the Turks.

1047
02:15:24,540 --> 02:15:26,541
What did Osman Bey do?

1048
02:15:26,541 --> 02:15:29,158
He ruled his lands with justice!

1049
02:15:29,158 --> 02:15:31,138
What did Osman Bey do?

1050
02:15:31,149 --> 02:15:34,021
He beat the tyrants!

1051
02:15:34,021 --> 02:15:35,979
What did Osman Bey do?

1052
02:15:35,979 --> 02:15:39,239
He spread the cause of the
Turks!

1053
02:15:39,241 --> 02:15:41,037
What did Osman Bey do!

1054
02:15:41,037 --> 02:15:44,177
Osman Bey conquered these lands!

1055
02:15:46,234 --> 02:15:48,034
What did Osman Bey do?

1056
02:15:48,065 --> 02:15:50,394
Osman Bey conquered hearts!

1057
02:15:50,394 --> 02:15:51,894
What did Osman Bey do?

1058
02:15:51,967 --> 02:15:55,527
Osman Bey built the foundations
of the new Turkic state!

1059
02:15:55,527 --> 02:15:58,495
Osman Bey searched for a sky
for his holy banner...

1060
02:15:58,495 --> 02:16:00,975
he looked for a place to wave it!

1061
02:16:01,514 --> 02:16:04,224
He searched for land to place
his flag!

1062
02:16:04,671 --> 02:16:09,011
He found it. Now, even if the whole world
unites, it makes no difference!

1063
02:16:09,308 --> 02:16:23,358
Long live Osman Bey!
Long live Osman Bey!

1064
02:16:27,860 --> 02:16:33,680
I'm Ertuğrul Ghazi's son,
Bey of the Kayı, Osman Bey!

1065
02:16:36,193 --> 02:16:41,674
Now, this village belongs to the Turks!

1066
02:17:07,901 --> 02:17:10,630
With strong horses...

1067
02:17:10,816 --> 02:17:14,066
brave alps...

1068
02:17:14,753 --> 02:17:18,213
we ran after a dream!

1069
02:17:19,985 --> 02:17:22,915
Now, thanks to Allah we reached
another point!

1070
02:17:23,235 --> 02:17:24,745
Thank Allah!

1071
02:17:24,745 --> 02:17:27,223
We expanded our home, thank Allah!

1072
02:17:27,223 --> 02:17:29,323
Thank Allah!

1073
02:17:29,404 --> 02:17:33,744
But this cause is greater
than one lifetime.

1074
02:17:34,293 --> 02:17:39,723
There are many other castles to conquer
and many other cities to control!

1075
02:17:41,507 --> 02:17:45,787
And there are many oppressed under
the rule of the tyrants!

1076
02:17:51,014 --> 02:17:56,424
But my sword of justice is closer to their
necks than ever!

1077
02:17:58,236 --> 02:18:00,367
Now, they all wait for their turn!

1078
02:18:04,196 --> 02:18:08,075
An order for the world,
peace for the hearts...

1079
02:18:08,163 --> 02:18:10,202
and pain for the heathens
is coming!

1080
02:18:10,932 --> 02:18:40,481
Allahu Akbar!
Allahu Akbar!

1081
02:18:40,481 --> 02:18:44,120
''Surely, we destined you a
decisive conquest.''

1082
02:18:49,237 --> 02:18:59,907
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com